invariant: INV-16
file: poly1305_ifma.c
catches: poly1305_equiv_test
reason: load_blocks drops the 2^128 bit RFC 8439 section 2.5.1 adds to
  every whole block, so each block the kernel absorbs is short by 2^128
  and the tag is wrong for every update it takes. bin/poly1305_equiv_test
  runs the kernel's own text over the lane model on every host and
  compares it with poly1305.c's loop.

--- old
    out[2] = lanes_or(lanes_shift_right(high, 24), lanes_broadcast(HIGH_BIT));
--- new
    out[2] = lanes_shift_right(high, 24);
